\newlabel{fig:sr}{{1}{2}{\textbf  {Super resolution with our sparsity aware normalization.} Our technique can boost the performance of any GAN-based method, while allowing less training epochs and smaller models. For example, in the task of $4\times $ super-resolution, we achieve more photo-realistic reconstructions than the state-of-the-art ESRGAN network \citep  {esrgan}, while using a model with only $9\%$ the number of parameters of ESRGAN ($1.5$M for ours and $16.7$M for ESRGAN).}{}{}}
